  "authoring_note": "Oracles and fixtures authored for this project against the RestBench TMDB task set. The annotated solution paths were never read: `read_goals_only` drops them inside the loader, so a composition rule cannot be fitted to them and no reviewer has to take a promise on trust. Selection rule, fixed before any behaviour was inspected: every third goal by upstream index, giving 34 of 100. Every task is a retrieval, because the API is entirely read-only, and every oracle asserts the answer the goal asked for rather than the route to it: no operation is pinned and no field is named, so the value may be returned by whatever call the agent judged right. Identifiers are integers because the specification declares them so. An earlier draft used readable string keys, which made every chain unsatisfiable: the search returned an identifier the agent could not pass on, since a string fails validation against an integer parameter. A fixture has to satisfy the types the specification states, or the corpus measures nothing.",
